    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.23,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.1,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 1.23 from 6 h onward. A plateau can be a true stationary phase or detector saturation, so I diluted the 18 h aliquot and scaled the readings back up. The 3x dilution gave 0.419, which is 1.26 OD. The 10x dilution gave 0.1325 and 0.1375, which is 1.35 OD. The 40x dilution gave 0.0276 and 0.0262, which is 1.08 OD. The undiluted reading was 1.21. The scaled values scatter around 1.2 with no monotonic rise as dilution increases. Saturation would make the scaled values climb with dilution. The replicate spread is about 4–5%, which accounts for the scatter. Reading and dilution agree, so biomass is as read, with an 18 h OD of about 1.2."
  },
